data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Mechanism:** Cas9 paired with a guide RNA cuts DNA at a chosen site [1]. Programmable cuts (double-strand breaks) allow insertion, deletion, modification, or replacement of DNA at that location [3].\n\n- **Biological origin:** CRISPR is adapted from a bacterial antiviral defense. Bacterial CRISPR sequences hold bacteriophage DNA and help destroy matching phage DNA in later infections [1][2].\n\n- **Hype versus evidence:** Headlines describe a breakthrough for many diseases [4] and HIV elimination [5]. The HIV result, however, was achieved only in cell culture, not in patients [5]."}

